From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Roman Leventov <leventov.ru@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 23:56:18 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 25/26] node-executor: add per-pool admission policy

Add a strict optional LOCAL_NODE_EXECUTOR_POOL_POLICIES map for independent-action concurrency, queue-warning thresholds, and elapsed event-loop unresponsiveness budgets on the default and named local Node pools.

Acquire dependency-aware pool capacity before the application-wide Node gate. Direct calls share one absolute admission deadline, while scheduled and cron work retains the existing pre-claim execution-start barrier and exact resident-generation reservation. Bounded dependency overflow preserves nested action progress without allowing executing work past the later global limit.

Make watchdog deadlines cover the first hanging probe and later failed intervals, while a timely successful health response disarms retirement even if the separate RSS read is still pending. Export bounded per-pool configuration, occupancy, wait-outcome, warning, and watchdog metrics.

Document the liveness properties, accepted scheduler head-of-line limitation, rollback contract, and rejected larger runtime designs.
